WEBVTT

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.733
<i>What's this feeling I have,</i>
<i>as if I'm looking forward to...</i>

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:25.939
<i>... somebody firing off his</i>
<i>missiles and ending everything?</i>

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:31.378
<i>Is it a bad thing, or is this normal?</i>

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:37.884
<i>I can't figure it out on my</i>
<i>own, so somebody tell me!</i>

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:43.490
<i>And that person I love has once again...</i>

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>... gone far away without anybody noticing.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:56.103
<i>Where have my dreams gone since then?</i>

00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:01.775
<i>I could swear that they</i>
<i>were right here long ago.</i>

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:07.814
<i>We had a love that set our hearts on fire.</i>

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:20.784
<i>Let's take back that feeling we had back then!</i>

00:02:08.308 --> 00:02:11.111
Hi, Washu here!

00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:12.612
Oh, Tenchi?

00:02:12.612 --> 00:02:17.384
U-Um, Washu... I was wondering
if you could do something for me.

00:02:17.384 --> 00:02:21.087
Oh, Tenchi, you little devil!

00:02:21.087 --> 00:02:24.558
I understand! Sleeping
alone on a night like this...

00:02:24.558 --> 00:02:28.528
Don't worry! I'll come right
over, and we can heat things up!

00:02:28.528 --> 00:02:31.097
That's not what I meant!

00:02:31.097 --> 00:02:34.734
Do you think you could take
down the Dimension Tunnel?

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:35.869
Huh?

00:02:35.869 --> 00:02:38.238
But why do you want it
taken down all of a sudden?

00:02:38.238 --> 00:02:41.441
I just think it isn't normal
for girls to keep popping up

00:02:41.441 --> 00:02:45.011
out of thin air in a guy's apartment.

00:02:45.011 --> 00:02:48.148
I understand. If that's
what you want, Tenchi.

00:02:48.148 --> 00:02:50.283
I'm sorry. I know I'm asking a lot.

00:02:50.283 --> 00:02:51.985
Don't mention it. It's no problem.

00:02:51.985 --> 00:02:53.787
'Bye, now.

00:02:53.787 --> 00:02:56.017
Thanks. Good night.

00:03:26.887 --> 00:03:30.457
All right, is everyone ready?

00:03:30.457 --> 00:03:31.992
<i>Miso</i> soup, check!

00:03:31.992 --> 00:03:34.528
Salmon and pickled vegetables, check!

00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:36.223
Ready over here, too!

00:03:38.164 --> 00:03:40.901
Dimension Tunnel, check!

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.869
All right, then, let's go to Tenchi's!

00:03:42.869 --> 00:03:44.268
Yeah!

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.288
- Ow!
- Wh-What in the world?

00:04:01.288 --> 00:04:03.085
The Dimension Tunnel!

00:04:12.465 --> 00:04:14.701
W-Washu...

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:18.138
Oh, no! The Dimension Tunnel is broken again!

00:04:18.138 --> 00:04:20.006
I closed it.

00:04:20.006 --> 00:04:21.808
- Huh?
- Y-You what?

00:04:21.808 --> 00:04:24.711
Why'd you do something so mean?

00:04:24.711 --> 00:04:29.149
Is it because I ate those chestnut
<i>imagawayaki</i> we have at teatime?

00:04:29.149 --> 00:04:32.218
Or because I tried on that
nurse uniform you like so much

00:04:32.218 --> 00:04:35.355
and stretched out the chest?

00:04:35.355 --> 00:04:39.559
Or did you do it because
I got your bio-computer drunk?

00:04:39.559 --> 00:04:42.629
- That's...
- Is that why you closed it?

00:04:42.629 --> 00:04:46.132
That's not...

00:04:46.132 --> 00:04:49.703
Tenchi called last night
and asked me to take it down.

00:04:49.703 --> 00:04:50.971
Lord Tenchi asked you to?

00:04:50.971 --> 00:04:53.173
But... But why?

00:04:53.173 --> 00:04:57.633
But the Dimension Tunnel is the
bond that keeps Tenchi and us together!

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:03.483
I'm sorry! I'm just hungry!

00:05:03.483 --> 00:05:07.287
You don't know the meaning
of the word "tension," do you?

00:05:07.287 --> 00:05:10.924
But for Lord Tenchi to
not want to eat breakfast...

00:05:10.924 --> 00:05:14.594
Unless! What if he's feeling sick?!

00:05:14.594 --> 00:05:17.330
Washu, what are you doing?!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.734
Hurry! Put the Dimension
Tunnel back the way it was!

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:23.328
He's not sick! Tenchi's...

00:05:33.313 --> 00:05:34.781
Here, Masaki!

00:05:34.781 --> 00:05:36.840
Thanks.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.458
What is it?

00:05:45.458 --> 00:05:49.292
I was just thinking how nice it is
to have a quiet breakfast like this.

00:05:51.498 --> 00:05:54.000
Wh-What?

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.869
Oh, it's nothing.

00:05:55.869 --> 00:05:57.771
Hey! Masaki!

00:05:57.771 --> 00:06:01.541
Let's go to school!

00:06:01.541 --> 00:06:04.344
Oh, no! Is it that late already?

00:06:04.344 --> 00:06:06.246
I have to go get ready!

00:06:06.246 --> 00:06:07.736
Sure...

00:06:13.386 --> 00:06:17.720
Tenchi... More...

00:06:21.261 --> 00:06:24.864
At any rate, we'll have
Lord Tenchi set the record straight.

00:06:24.864 --> 00:06:27.634
But how?

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.870
How else? We'll go to Tokyo.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.541
No. We're in the red this month.
We don't have that kind of money.

00:06:34.541 --> 00:06:37.410
In that case, we'll just have to have
the party to blame for this incident

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.880
take responsibility for it.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.016
M-Me?

00:06:43.016 --> 00:06:47.987
That's right. All of this happened
because of your meddling, Father!

00:06:47.987 --> 00:06:50.390
I did what I thought was best for my son!

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:55.528
So you're saying that you
don't care at all about us?

00:06:55.528 --> 00:06:58.231
N-No, I'm not saying that at all!

00:06:58.231 --> 00:07:01.564
Mr. Masaki, give us train fare!

00:07:05.438 --> 00:07:09.075
B-But I can't give you that kind of
money, not on what I make a month...

00:07:09.075 --> 00:07:11.839
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

00:07:15.482 --> 00:07:19.152
All right, pay attention, now!

00:07:19.152 --> 00:07:23.123
Now, let's say that this is
Nobuyuki's monthly salary.

00:07:23.123 --> 00:07:27.060
This part is his taxes, and this
is what goes into the household.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:31.998
If we subtract the cost of his monthly
girls' comics, his twice-weekly drinking,

00:07:31.998 --> 00:07:37.303
his cigarettes, sports papers, and
the fruit milk he has after his baths,

00:07:37.303 --> 00:07:40.373
he has this much left over.

00:07:40.373 --> 00:07:42.575
And if we then multiply this by 12,

00:07:42.575 --> 00:07:46.379
and again by the number of
years Nobuyuki has worked, we get...

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:48.314
Um... Let's <i>see...</i>

00:07:48.314 --> 00:07:52.852
We find that he has saved enough to
buy round-trip tickets on the red-eye bus

00:07:52.852 --> 00:07:55.755
from Okayama to Tokyo for
five adults, one child, and one pet,

00:07:55.755 --> 00:08:00.059
plus 500 yen for lunches and snacks.

00:08:00.059 --> 00:08:02.220
Well? Did you follow me?

00:08:03.963 --> 00:08:06.299
Oh, so that's how it is!

00:08:06.299 --> 00:08:09.369
Well, what do you know?
He really did have it!

00:08:09.369 --> 00:08:11.604
Now that we know, let's start
searching the house right away!

00:08:11.604 --> 00:08:14.539
Now we can go to Tenchi's!

00:08:14.874 --> 00:08:17.777
I was certainly worried for a while there!

00:08:17.777 --> 00:08:20.337
The money I had stashed away!

00:08:21.981 --> 00:08:26.418
"Tenmangu High School
White Phoenix Festival"

00:08:26.619 --> 00:08:29.455
Did you see yesterday's
women's wrestling match, Masaki?

00:08:29.455 --> 00:08:30.690
- Sakuya!
- It was awesome!

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:32.025
- Good morning!
- Sadako lkarinu went in and...

00:08:32.025 --> 00:08:34.761
'Morning! All we have left to do
today is buy the ingredients, right?

00:08:34.761 --> 00:08:36.729
I think so.

00:08:36.729 --> 00:08:40.200
So I hear Sakuya made a
boxed lunch for you, huh, Masaki?

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.768
Uh... Yeah.

00:08:41.768 --> 00:08:43.269
And?

00:08:43.269 --> 00:08:44.470
And what?

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.306
Oh, come on!

00:08:46.306 --> 00:08:48.408
I'm asking you if you told her how you feel.

00:08:48.408 --> 00:08:51.044
Huh? But I...

00:08:51.044 --> 00:08:53.179
Then you'll have to settle it tomorrow.

00:08:53.179 --> 00:08:55.682
Tomorrow? Does it have something
to do with the School Festival?

00:08:55.682 --> 00:08:58.651
No, the Wrap Party afterwards!

00:08:58.651 --> 00:09:01.888
There's a legend at this school
that couples who profess their love

00:09:01.888 --> 00:09:04.924
at the Wrap Party always stay together.

00:09:04.924 --> 00:09:06.693
- Huh?
- Gross!

00:09:06.693 --> 00:09:08.027
Isn't it?

00:09:08.027 --> 00:09:10.864
Telling her at the Wrap Party...

00:09:10.864 --> 00:09:16.461
Masaki! Let's go see the girls'
wrestling club practice after school!

00:09:24.677 --> 00:09:28.114
Just a little more. Just a little
more, and they'll all come together.

00:09:28.114 --> 00:09:30.139
And when they do...

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:34.954
What is it, Masaki?

00:09:34.954 --> 00:09:36.723
Oh, it's nothing.

00:09:36.723 --> 00:09:39.859
There's a legend at this school
that couples who profess their love

00:09:39.859 --> 00:09:43.129
at the Wrap Party always stay together.

00:09:43.129 --> 00:09:44.898
Let's just bring up the drums and amp!

00:09:44.898 --> 00:09:46.365
Sure!

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:49.669
There's a wrinkle over there!
Spread it out right!

00:09:49.669 --> 00:09:51.371
Right!

00:09:51.371 --> 00:09:53.373
Gross, this is filthy! What is it?

00:09:53.373 --> 00:09:55.174
It must've belonged to one of
the upperclassmen who graduated.

00:09:55.174 --> 00:09:56.776
Just throw it away!

00:09:56.776 --> 00:09:58.471
Yeah, you're right...

00:10:05.118 --> 00:10:07.020
Here's the fryer for the crêpes!

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:08.688
Okay, good job.

00:10:08.688 --> 00:10:10.790
Take care of the settings, too, okay, Masaki?

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:11.691
Sure.

00:10:11.691 --> 00:10:13.860
I'll help!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.864
Oh, right. The executive
committee wanted to see me.

00:10:17.864 --> 00:10:18.631
I'll be back later.

00:10:18.631 --> 00:10:20.462
See you later!

00:10:23.002 --> 00:10:27.307
I'm hungry, so I think I'll go to the
cafeteria and have some hashed rice!

00:10:27.307 --> 00:10:31.945
Um... I'll go to the co-op
and buy some magic markers!

00:10:31.945 --> 00:10:33.212
See you later...

00:10:33.212 --> 00:10:35.114
Hey, could you take out the nuts?

00:10:35.114 --> 00:10:36.945
Sure!

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:43.222
Watching those two is so frustrating...

00:10:43.222 --> 00:10:44.958
Get your act together, Masaki!

00:10:44.958 --> 00:10:47.593
Be a man and take the plunge! Be a man!

00:10:47.593 --> 00:10:49.262
Could you hold that for me?

00:10:49.262 --> 00:10:50.196
Like this?

00:10:50.196 --> 00:10:52.999
Okay, things are looking good so far...

00:10:52.999 --> 00:10:57.737
Masaki! Let's go watch the
girls' wrestling club practice!

00:10:57.737 --> 00:11:00.467
That stupid, meddling jerk!

00:11:03.576 --> 00:11:07.680
That boy is a nuisance, all right.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.114
You know what to do? Go!

00:11:23.162 --> 00:11:25.732
Looks like everybody's busy...

00:11:25.732 --> 00:11:28.360
Now, where'd I put that nut?

00:11:31.504 --> 00:11:34.701
Here you go! Am I considerate, or what?

00:11:37.243 --> 00:11:40.474
German suplex!

00:11:42.248 --> 00:11:44.876
Huh? Where'd Amagasaki go?

00:11:58.598 --> 00:12:02.557
What's this wonderful
sensation that's running up my back?

00:12:08.074 --> 00:12:10.907
Maybe I overslept a little...

00:12:12.178 --> 00:12:14.544
What the heck?!

00:12:17.517 --> 00:12:19.318
What the heck happened?

00:12:19.318 --> 00:12:21.587
Did a burglar get in here or something?

00:12:21.587 --> 00:12:23.723
No, that's not it...

00:12:23.723 --> 00:12:25.291
It's not here...

00:12:25.291 --> 00:12:28.661
That's strange, we searched the whole house...

00:12:28.661 --> 00:12:31.064
I wonder where he hid it?

00:12:31.064 --> 00:12:33.666
You're awake, Ryoko?

00:12:33.666 --> 00:12:36.294
What's going on around here?

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.906
Oh, okay... So that's what's going on.

00:12:39.906 --> 00:12:43.976
Come, Ryoko, help us look for Father's money!

00:12:43.976 --> 00:12:45.244
Get real...

00:12:45.244 --> 00:12:46.512
What?

00:12:46.512 --> 00:12:50.450
Tenchi and I are bound by true love.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:54.087
Distance doesn't make any difference.

00:12:54.087 --> 00:12:55.855
What's with that attitude of hers?!

00:12:55.855 --> 00:12:58.124
Fine!

00:12:58.124 --> 00:13:02.328
We'll find it by ourselves!

00:13:02.328 --> 00:13:04.694
I'm still in the same pinch!

00:13:07.366 --> 00:13:07.600
"Crêpes"

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.801
"Crêpes"
I'm back!

00:13:08.801 --> 00:13:10.036
"Crêpes"
Hi!

00:13:10.036 --> 00:13:12.371
"Crêpes"
The crêpes fryer is all set.

00:13:12.371 --> 00:13:13.306
"Crêpes"
Thanks!

00:13:13.306 --> 00:13:16.342
"Crêpes"
Okay, then, let's get
everything ready for tomorrow!

00:13:16.342 --> 00:13:16.843
Okay, then, let's get
everything ready for tomorrow!

00:13:16.843 --> 00:13:19.679
Sakuya, will you go buy
the ingredients for the crêpes?

00:13:19.679 --> 00:13:20.780
Sure! No problem!

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:24.917
Masaki, Sakuya will have trouble
by herself, so give her a hand.

00:13:24.917 --> 00:13:26.886
Sure. Want to get going, then?

00:13:26.886 --> 00:13:27.887
Sure.

00:13:27.887 --> 00:13:30.823
See you later!

00:13:30.823 --> 00:13:32.792
Are you okay? It's not too heavy?

00:13:32.792 --> 00:13:34.861
No, I'm fine.

00:13:34.861 --> 00:13:36.462
Masaki?

00:13:36.462 --> 00:13:38.698
Don't you think the girls
are acting kind of strange?

00:13:38.698 --> 00:13:41.067
Now that you mention it,
it's like they've been

00:13:41.067 --> 00:13:44.036
going out of their way to get us alone.

00:13:44.036 --> 00:13:49.408
If that's true, it's great. It's let me
spend just more time alone with you.

00:13:49.408 --> 00:13:51.811
Masaki!

00:13:51.811 --> 00:13:54.847
Hey!

00:13:54.847 --> 00:13:56.048
Th-There it is again...

00:13:56.048 --> 00:13:59.285
Axe bomber!

00:13:59.285 --> 00:14:01.821
I knew it!

00:14:01.821 --> 00:14:03.311
Huh?

00:14:10.696 --> 00:14:13.065
I just can't find it...

00:14:13.065 --> 00:14:16.125
I'm dead on my feet...

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.540
Let's just give up...

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:24.677
No way! Not when the honor
of the Galaxy Police is at stake!

00:14:24.677 --> 00:14:27.046
Come to think of it, where's Washu?

00:14:27.046 --> 00:14:29.148
Now that you mention it...

00:14:29.148 --> 00:14:31.017
She went and disappeared...

00:14:31.017 --> 00:14:33.186
I'm right here.

00:14:33.186 --> 00:14:35.381
Wh-Wha...

00:14:44.063 --> 00:14:46.554
Wh-What in the world is this?

00:14:47.567 --> 00:14:54.974
This is Pochi, a self-propelled treasure
finding and excavating dog machine.

00:14:54.974 --> 00:14:56.142
- He's so cute!
- He's so cute!

00:14:56.142 --> 00:14:57.643
- What's cute?
- What's cute?

00:14:57.643 --> 00:14:57.777
"This part is cute"
- What's cute?
- What's cute?

00:14:57.777 --> 00:15:03.115
"This part is cute"
He uses his dowsing abilities to
locate items that people have hidden.

00:15:03.115 --> 00:15:05.117
"This part is cute"
He'll find that money in no time!

00:15:05.117 --> 00:15:05.518
"This one is too"
He'll find that money in no time!

00:15:05.518 --> 00:15:09.045
"This one is too"

00:15:09.255 --> 00:15:11.314
Somehow, this isn't making
me any more confident...

00:15:14.126 --> 00:15:15.895
We bought the ingredients for the crêpes!

00:15:15.895 --> 00:15:17.296
Okay, good job.

00:15:17.296 --> 00:15:21.500
Sorry, but could you put up
posters all over school, Sakuya?

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.001
Sure.

00:15:22.001 --> 00:15:25.304
They're heavy, so you give her a hand, Masaki.

00:15:25.304 --> 00:15:26.472
Uh... Sure.

00:15:26.472 --> 00:15:30.543
Oh, and could you hang this from the roof?

00:15:30.543 --> 00:15:32.745
Thanks!

00:15:32.745 --> 00:15:35.081
The roof should be deserted now.

00:15:35.081 --> 00:15:39.051
Masaki, this is your big chance.
It's all up to you now.

00:15:39.051 --> 00:15:41.621
Forget about tomorrow,
make your move now!

00:15:41.621 --> 00:15:44.423
Masaki, go for it!

00:15:44.423 --> 00:15:47.627
Where in the world did he hide it?

00:15:47.627 --> 00:15:49.662
Hm?

00:15:49.662 --> 00:15:53.928
This is my lucky day! I can buy
seven packages of salted kelp with this!

00:16:00.873 --> 00:16:04.309
Pochi, come with me, please...

00:16:08.481 --> 00:16:10.850
I've always been the victor.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:15.621
And no opponent has ever taken me down.

00:16:15.621 --> 00:16:17.990
But is that really for the best?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:22.028
A female professional wrestler slams
into her opponent with all her strength

00:16:22.028 --> 00:16:24.597
and uses her whole body to
counter her opponent's moves.

00:16:24.597 --> 00:16:26.997
But I...

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.472
Masaki! Where's Masaki?!

00:16:33.472 --> 00:16:37.977
That man! He took a beating
from me and he's still running around!

00:16:37.977 --> 00:16:41.777
Could he be the man who
will make my wish come true?!

00:16:44.016 --> 00:16:47.787
No doubt about it...
Something is happening to my body.

00:16:47.787 --> 00:16:51.691
Something inside me is howling...

00:16:51.691 --> 00:16:53.955
I have to tell Masaki!

00:16:55.795 --> 00:16:57.863
Masaki!

00:16:57.863 --> 00:17:00.331
Elbow crush!

00:17:02.001 --> 00:17:05.037
Hey! Masaki!

00:17:05.037 --> 00:17:07.505
Brain buster!

00:17:08.507 --> 00:17:12.011
Hey! Masaki!

00:17:12.011 --> 00:17:15.174
Flying cross chop!

00:17:16.849 --> 00:17:21.420
Hey... Masaki...

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:24.514
Giant swing!

00:17:41.874 --> 00:17:45.144
I'm fighting against a powerful enemy...

00:17:45.144 --> 00:17:49.740
My five senses are humming and
screaming, and my blood is boiling!

00:17:51.851 --> 00:17:55.412
Masaki! Watch me fight!

00:17:59.492 --> 00:18:01.084
I knew you'd come.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.627
This is the last time.

00:18:09.268 --> 00:18:11.395
Drop kick!

00:18:16.675 --> 00:18:19.645
Get up! Get up, Amagasaki!

00:18:19.645 --> 00:18:21.613
M-Masaki...

00:18:22.348 --> 00:18:25.384
Don't give up, Amagasaki!

00:18:25.384 --> 00:18:27.875
L-I can hear them all...

00:18:30.589 --> 00:18:32.784
Go for it, Amagasaki!

00:18:56.816 --> 00:19:00.445
He... He did a Counter-Lariat...

00:19:07.526 --> 00:19:12.097
It's over now. It's all over.

00:19:12.097 --> 00:19:14.691
I finally got my wish...

00:19:32.618 --> 00:19:34.245
Ow...

00:19:36.722 --> 00:19:39.558
A-Amagasaki! It's not what you think!

00:19:39.558 --> 00:19:42.027
Hey, what's the big idea?

00:19:42.027 --> 00:19:44.730
All you had to do was tell
me you'd be busy up here!

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:49.335
Don't worry, I won't tell anybody.
Am I considerate, or what?

00:19:49.335 --> 00:19:53.635
Amagasaki! It's not what you think!

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.449
Th-This...

00:20:03.449 --> 00:20:07.453
It is! It's Sadako lkarinu's mask!
The Masked Wrestler!

00:20:07.453 --> 00:20:11.490
And it's the ultra-rare one
she wore in her debut match!

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:13.754
Awesome!

00:20:19.265 --> 00:20:22.668
Um... Have you found my money yet?

00:20:22.668 --> 00:20:24.503
No, it's hopeless...

00:20:24.503 --> 00:20:27.165
Really? Thank goodness...

00:20:43.289 --> 00:20:44.950
Tomorrow...

00:20:53.332 --> 00:20:56.001
Couples that profess
their love at the Wrap Party

00:20:56.001 --> 00:20:58.936
always stay together, huh?

00:21:00.205 --> 00:21:03.766
Everything will finally
start to fall apart tomorrow...

00:21:36.875 --> 00:21:40.479
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:40.479 --> 00:21:44.383
<i>Sleeping late, staying up late,</i>
<i>and napping all the time!</i>

00:21:44.383 --> 00:21:47.987
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:47.987 --> 00:21:51.924
<i>Sneaking bites to eat, midnight</i>
<i>snacks, and pouring tea on my rice!</i>

00:21:51.924 --> 00:21:55.427
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:55.427 --> 00:21:59.398
<i>Playing video games and singing karaoke!</i>

00:21:59.398 --> 00:22:02.735
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:22:02.735 --> 00:22:06.739
<i>Lying in the sun and taking baths outside!</i>

00:22:06.739 --> 00:22:08.874
<i>- Taking side trips!</i>
<i>- Gossiping!</i>

00:22:08.874 --> 00:22:10.809
<i>- Taking long baths</i>
<i>- Wasting my money!</i>

00:22:10.809 --> 00:22:12.311
<i>- Being a busybody!</i>
<i>- Talking forever on the phone!</i>

00:22:12.311 --> 00:22:18.150
<i>- Unrequited love!</i>
<i>- Stealing other people's men!</i>

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:22.254
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:22.254 --> 00:22:25.524
<i>no matter how old I get!</i>

00:22:25.524 --> 00:22:29.061
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:29.061 --> 00:22:33.760
<i>even if I die, change shape, or get reborn!</i>

00:22:42.474 --> 00:22:44.910
Hey, I'm Ryoko.

00:22:44.910 --> 00:22:48.747
Tenchi, you aren't being
seduced by Sakuya, are you?

00:22:48.747 --> 00:22:52.017
Ayeka and the others went
there because they were worried.

00:22:52.017 --> 00:22:54.953
But I have faith in you.

00:22:54.953 --> 00:22:57.189
Well, I think it'll be a royal
pain to have to deal with Ayeka

00:22:57.189 --> 00:23:00.092
and that School Festival
thing of yours, Tenchi.

00:23:00.092 --> 00:23:05.664
Oh, well. Let's go out on another
date sometime, okay, Tenchi?

00:23:05.664 --> 00:23:11.159
Next time on
<i>Tenchi in Tokyo:</i> "Carnival!"
